{"name":"Range Land","hex":"#68bd56","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"range","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A line or series of mountains, buildings, etc.","A fireplace; a fire or other cooking apparatus; now specifically, a large cooking stove with many burners (hotplates)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel over (an area, etc); to roam, wander. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To rove over or through."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/range"},{"term":"land","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of Earth which is not covered by oceans or other bodies of water.","Real estate or landed property; a partitioned and measurable area which is owned and acquired and on which buildings and structures can be built and erected."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To descend to a surface, especially from the air.","To alight, to descend from a vehicle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land"}],"entries":[{"title":"Range Land","blocks":[{"text":"Range Land is a 1949 American Western film directed by Lambert Hillyer and written by Adele Buffington. The film stars Whip Wilson, Andy Clyde, Reno Browne, Leonard Penn, Reed Howes and Kenne Duncan. The film was released on December 24, 1949, by Monogram Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3b/Range_Land_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Range_Land","wikidata":"Q15704010"},{"title":"Rangeland","blocks":[{"text":"Rangelands are grasslands, shrublands, woodlands, wetlands, and deserts that are grazed by domestic livestock or wild animals. Types of rangelands include tallgrass and shortgrass prairies, desert grasslands and shrublands, woodlands, savannas, chaparrals, steppes, open forest, and tundras. Rangelands do not include forests lacking grazable understory vegetation, barren desert, farmland, or land covered by solid rock, concrete, or glaciers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Muddy_Water_Red_desert.jpg/330px-Muddy_Water_Red_desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rangeland","wikidata":"Q3364870"},{"title":"Land","blocks":[{"text":"Land, also known as dry land, ground, or earth, is the solid terrestrial surface of Earth not submerged by the ocean or another body of water. It makes up approximately 29% of Earth's surface and includes all continents and islands. Earth's land surface is almost entirely covered by regolith, a layer of rock, soil, and minerals that forms the outer part of the crust. Land plays an important role in Earth's climate system, being involved in the carbon cycle, nitrogen cycle, and water cycle. One-third of land is covered in trees another third is used for agriculture, and roughly one-tenth is covered in glacier ice. The remainder consists of desert, savannah, and prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg/330px-Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land","wikidata":"Q11081619"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Salsola_tragus_monoculture_post_restoration.JPG/500px-Salsola_tragus_monoculture_post_restoration.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Salsola_tragus_monoculture_post_restoration.JPG/500px-Salsola_tragus_monoculture_post_restoration.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Weeds are all that remains in Idaho after a failed restoration project following wildfire,  and subsequent invasion by non-native species. Russian thistle (Salsola tragus) is the only plant species seen in this picture.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalsola_tragus_monoculture_post_restoration.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Rangeworld545.png/500px-Rangeworld545.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Rangeworld545.png/1280px-Rangeworld545.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Rangeworld545.png/500px-Rangeworld545.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map showing the world's rangelands, and areas that are not rangeland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARangeworld545.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Cattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg/500px-Cattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Cattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg/1280px-Cattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Cattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg/500px-Cattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cattle on savanna rangeland in Namibia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACattle_standing_on_Namibian_rangeland.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Palouse_from_Steptoe_Butte.jpg/120px-Palouse_from_Steptoe_Butte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Palouse_from_Steptoe_Butte.jpg/250px-Palou